<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Adrian Pelt</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1892–1981</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Adrian Pelt was a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> journalist and international civil servant who served as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-nations">United Nations</a> Commissioner in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/libya">Libya</a> from 1950 to 1951. He guided the drafting of a federal constitution and the creation of the government that led Libya to independence as the United Kingdom of Libya under King Idris in December 1951.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/adrian-pelt.jpg" alt="Adrian Pelt" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown photographer (Dutch Rijksvoorlichtingsdienst RVD) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:AdriaanPelt.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
